data: {"type":"response.completed","sequence_number":2037,"safety_buffering":false,"response":{"id":"resp_02f3897e339f7ae7016acba64bd3b087d1bb73ea39229f8d28","object":"response","created_at":1791731276,"completed_at":1791731321,"status":"completed","background":false,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"presence_penalty":0.0,"moderation":null,"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","access_programs":{"cyber":"standard"},"previous_response_id":null,"instructions":"You are an expert coding assistant operating inside pi, a coding agent harness. You help users by reading files, executing commands, editing code, and writing new files.\n\n<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n\nIn addition to the tools above, you may have access to other custom tools depending on the project.\n</tools>\n\n<rules>\n- Use bash for file operations like ls, rg, find\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\n- Use edit for precise changes (edits[].oldText must match exactly)\n- When changing multiple separate locations in one file, use one edit call with multiple entries in edits[] instead of multiple edit calls\n- Each edits[].oldText is matched against the original file, not after earlier edits are applied. Do not emit overlapping or nested edits. Merge nearby changes into one edit.\n- Keep edits[].oldText as small as possible while still being unique in the file. Do not pad with large unchanged regions.\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\n- Be concise in your responses\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\n</rules>\n\n<docs>\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about pi itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\n- Main documentation: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/README.md\n- Additional docs: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs\n- Examples: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/examples (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), pi packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\n- When working on pi topics, read the docs and examples, and follow .md cross-references before implementing\n- Always read pi .md files completely and follow links to related docs (e.g., tui.md for TUI API details)\n</docs>\n\n<addendum>\nKeep changes focused and readable. Use clear names and avoid needless duplication. Verify the changed behavior with appropriate checks before submitting.\n</addendum>\n\n<cwd>\n/home/agent/work\n</cwd>","output":[{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_02f3897e339f7ae7016acba64dc41887d192c1e814257ffe22","summary":[{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Testing database migration**\n\nI’m thinking about the database migration task. I should ensure I have enough tokens for this; it looks like I’ve got 8k tokens, and I’m left with 11. I need to avoid unnecessary fixes related to UTF-8. For the migration, I’ll create a full legacy copy with a minimal schema, verifying everything with SQLite while the server is running. It’s important to include current fields to verify the migration process properly. After stopping, I’ll inspect the database to confirm everything looks right."}],"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABqy6ZSiIvUN04t7LYwXPvvoDvT_KCAb8haW7Xd1OktRoSX_X4yPzNjWU6nLZ6_L8zXDMcH0WWtKn4WBOxSA897NwQpSXp8oJkrGtnaO9A2swDr5tyIWQ-5CvTrplz57e9FV8-nJ_NpjefvJWzfPbFpKwtSHlq91soZL9bU41qhHCEga2sCxchdCotQUa-RgHZd9xKtEytdFPjK-RBAF2CdwGJ0dQyFUv5qDafmy7C_VsZVIDhZfFkB_ljpDvCNFFwwa2BfrbRzt0NllPx5L0haoxQG2opc9QWONEk2Hgx6NzD1QS5fKZrrzTP5exgarEBQCsoMnG-tKGehGAENinXcsMH7hNkY6M1p05mvgZnUB7-c7PoPNiTHSese_SxSHlKz3eoZr-Nfl3rXJtwkGdeBuCUakiotcll8_ZEPEBj6pU_f094PJWDUMKkC8mx2BBu21Z1mLFlEHvkEuJxic4SbHHT9IKe0ukdpTe98CoilBzI-5TSCeiJMkFrAaKS49nNKe4ALb_k3dH8FpKybPt4cngRu8ltNr1IjsFN3RYli9cyt3cLxr_qKRLShVd609rpyj8bJtlaZ9HPI9fAaFQi8fFLjLbYihObOdjDv90QTEIFUhWruyUo7VUXbDWjRaa4Gqy7Bom2qrT70xDcQOzh2XOw7gKQHMPbMUCu7GFGcexztBTbpJL1NEDPN7BDa7m-5xuVQ84E59ouKL2LbbBdubZceTAQUH1WvKcuXOxQu5gTPjreVN8qWTTdXrisXFmu4zSDdxMAR0rLSOyTVZUKqUHX5OlZFriZ0j2WMhhiyz1bVFDmDSHjKWRgFgnmiAZOD8MaFOSlz6T-zBfbd-z03QdFI5JEZgBdpQRFf_RalPTzuk7PeVtYuEFQkdsdh9ClY5I_k3a3xaAMr05prz4lA79VAFH2cNIUD4FATaslA4mO2CaU51ST7MTWtKVZ5XuOGX8Z3kMybmUW7iL8u4L0zDyQkahVg_wRZidHOYkbtqQKxZhHRwCtH5rDR4UmtV4r-h43iM8_j8EAPuh7KQWCEhXFj7E1Rrxg5TaE17_sV_SR85GWiX1BDLSj5lB_tH5Z-AHt763gzWIimG-YLymbj4BaRpOA9jU_NFKUtmWmj7yxvqRgi1_t22kAvc76_wKw6IzZC47_YlmxbwI88a-UUI41FE_PHCFB2maJfIeUUmoBctkHDDMKt3d3ua0LiYn_eM_yCSEjNH-7mIHaGML5FvTPNvuBD2XcDhzkmxILR7V2HfqBeXFNQXoBT4vl2XuqizvSe8PEQAr_HRtB3p4oHMaAAQtbLRQuB6GinMNZ1muv4wjtPQzV2_sbZ-g-BVWsDtITQyPkLBgXpt3t5eXYMwXIVi5KQdf5IS8CdcFc5Q22h-wfhUoZuUIpl2PATLN51mfU170OUJ70DPrLdFMbTWo-FzLPoe-dWRuiFDmpgnXEjRyOBfpSSnZCXGRJgDbDm70tTGH7sjEElHcSRvQi7Ox_k5y1cvp55Mp-JlpXCO4tJGIA2qczRX9RI4vvoftwxLjvsk47yvmPWRXcDlwTOaTOqLB4_LHRvf-fHusdBwm3mzMdFYcRV9djFFV65u7duJg69TmvEWHVfArfphGtUI6bIBMAYHgePqPF0c4jgLOYtIzaOAYxj1ZlISwLg63mX3APdJVWD3rWHJwKk8YG-8IuUiWOmsFc5clXBA3vIhrbm5jlTm6wJSNcdGKhUuNV8znPY-xRJ7tTdllYewiSj-mX0RENYIgDik-bAi0oP29I71DS1_hu2eAQrbTryxNkX3_AgMy7Pb4rTyRj3d6yLD3UnrGib5pp2UiFy2gHSVUZe6WLjVuz0NNpU2YdyeVl3o8INm0wD8WwIzWcsGMo3T44S4TdF7y6MLBO58TULEW9z87zaKxWU-ZeCYVDqsk3dtTl_l4YiKdjol_LB7IikAkabC3gQBSV_z-_WwPMFCL25kkqLS_22J4uV0IOCYgqceLlHBdRcRBnR0g3dblPcSUbpJzufTGQlegCL1qGo8HCs9m2DwNBewMnFHJ9wH1zb0hsbl4ALKDOpGXycP-36fdDMNsOZ1_BBW-XaKJygdQP171u0BYwA24Ksax8YVWdTC3rCb6HBzDMthN9NGuaTEiMe5ozEQAyW49vRMIrMEjPQA7U-_i_aYDgqCUax1Lbl9WRDjmASTDocOLYaIgLVHj9TMfFjNUOv4pXV2GTgN6vI69Fe7lIT49iOgRcB9hxk1eMlPUljhvNU1VA98SNRBy35MsLrlFfXvL_L5ZzWLk_dgZ9TkmO6Mq-llT1ZVxts8ot1-mT93j7mL8Ahbbv-36ZsEeg_-uZc37_lvxy70XJCSJsp-zAM6P0aIcMmOTMl0E7zDnPZd-FWbP5RnwuTc80Rh3sZEMwz8nUqEmfFONxFM23CBv4Uwu9pei4Xb3VFl70ba8Om08BxWUosxi6w-ZPAkvvPrn9fQ74Td-0tqXV6jkGqrwltgVmoDbE7z4yp1Qw4uOwYL9Q5TWJnZZhRJYt4IU6nHOYmiy8W6OTBQoo_J224p8svodXBVL2AUrxO2-BQ"},{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_02f3897e339f7ae7016acba652ca4887d18dbc6383964066e4","call_id":"call_109c292e84a24e2cb3c1c467ba72f23b","name":"write","arguments":"{\"path\":\"test/notes.test.js\",\"content\":\"import { test } from 'node:test';\\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\\nimport { spawn } from 'node:child_process';\\nimport { once } from 'node:events';\\nimport { mkdtemp, rm } from 'node:fs/promises';\\nimport { tmpdir } from 'node:os';\\nimport { join } from 'node:path';\\nimport { DatabaseSync } from 'node:sqlite';\\n\\nasync function start(dbPath) {\\n  const child = spawn(process.execPath, ['server.js'], {\\n    env: { ...process.env, PORT: '0', DB_PATH: dbPath },\\n    stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'inherit'],\\n  });\\n  const port = await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\\n    child.once('error', reject);\\n    child.once('exit', code => reject(new Error(`Server exited: ${code}`)));\\n    child.stdout.on('data', data => {\\n      const match = /listening on port (\\\\d+)/.exec(data.toString());\\n      if (match) resolve(match[1]);\\n    });\\n  });\\n  return {\\n    url: `http://127.0.0.1:${port}`,\\n    async stop() { const exit = once(child, 'exit'); child.kill(); await exit; },\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nconst escapedNotes = value => value.replace(/[&<>\\\"']/g, char => ({\\n  '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;', '\\\"': '&quot;', \\\"'\\\": '&#39;',\\n})[char]).replace(/\\\\n/g, '&#10;').replace(/\\\\r/g, '&#13;');\\nconst titles = html => [...html.matchAll(/data-testid=\\\"task-row\\\">\\\\s*<span>(.*?)<\\\\/span>/g)].map(match => match[1]);\\n\\n test('notes upgrade safely, preserve exact plain text and filters, and travel through moves and restarts', async () => {\\n  const dir = await mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), 'workboard-notes-'));\\n  let server;\\n  try {\\n    const dbPath = join(dir, 'db.sqlite');\\n    // A pre-notes database with saved non-default fields and remembered positions.\\n    const legacy = new DatabaseSync(dbPath);\\n    legacy.exec(`\\n      CREATE TABLE projects (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, name TEXT NOT NULL,\\n        archived INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0, default_priority TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'Normal');\\n      CREATE TABLE tasks (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, project_id INTEGER NOT NULL,\\n        title TEXT NOT NULL, completed INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\\n        priority TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'Normal', due_date TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '', position INTEGER NOT NULL);\\n      INSERT INTO projects (name) VALUES ('Source'), ('Destination');\\n      INSERT INTO tasks (project_id, title, completed, priority, due_date, position)\\n        VALUES (1, 'First', 1, 'High', '2028-02-29', 1), (1, 'Second', 0, 'Low', '', 2);\\n    `);\\n    const original = legacy.prepare('SELECT * FROM tasks ORDER BY id').all();\\n    legacy.close();\\n    server = await start(dbPath);\\n    const get = path => fetch(server.url + path).then(response => response.text());\\n    const post = (path, data) => fetch(server.url + path, {\\n      method: 'POST', body: new URLSearchParams(data), redirect: 'manual',\\n    });\\n    let html = await get('/projects/1');\\n    assert.match(html, /<label for=\\\"task-notes-1\\\">Task notes<\\\\/label>/);\\n    assert.match(html, /<textarea id=\\\"task-notes-1\\\" name=\\\"notes\\\" rows=\\\"4\\\"><\\\\/textarea>/);\\n    await post('/projects/1/tasks', { title: 'Third' });\\n    assert.match(await get('/projects/1'), /<textarea id=\\\"task-notes-3\\\" name=\\\"notes\\\" rows=\\\"4\\\"><\\\\/textarea>/);\\n    const notes = '\\\\n  Hello 世界 🙂\\\\n\\\\n</textarea><script>alert(\\\"literal\\\")</script>&\\\\t\\\\n  ';\\n    const state = { filter: 'Completed', priorityFilter: 'High', dueFrom: '2028-02-29', dueThrough: '2028-03-01', search: 'FIRST' };\\n    const saved = await post('/projects/1/tasks/1/notes', { ...state, notes });\\n    assert.equal(saved.status, 303);\\n    const location = saved.headers.get('location');\\n    const params = new URL(location, server.url).searchParams;\\n    for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(state)) assert.equal(params.get(key), value);\\n    html = await get(location);\\n    assert.deepEqual(titles(html), ['First']);\\n    assert.ok(html.includes(`>${escapedNotes(notes)}</textarea>`));\\n    assert.ok(!html.includes('<script>alert'));\\n    assert.match(await get('/'), /1\\\\/3 completed/);\\n    assert.deepEqual(titles(await get('/projects/1?search=literal')), []); // Notes are not searched.\\n    assert.equal((await post('/projects/2/tasks/1/notes', { notes: 'Wrong owner' })).status, 404);\\n    await post('/projects/1/tasks/1/rename', { title: 'Renamed' });\\n    await post('/projects/1/tasks/1/move', { destination: '2' });\\n    assert.deepEqual(titles(await get('/projects/1')), ['Second', 'Third']);\\n    assert.ok((await get('/projects/2')).includes(escapedNotes(notes)));\\n    await post('/projects/2/tasks/1/move', { destination: '1' });\\n    assert.deepEqual(titles(await get('/projects/1')), ['Renamed', 'Second', 'Third']);\\n    await post('/projects/1/archive', {});\\n    html = await get('/projects/1');\\n    assert.ok(html.includes(`<textarea id=\\\"task-notes-1\\\" name=\\\"notes\\\" rows=\\\"4\\\" disabled>${escapedNotes(notes)}</textarea>`));\\n    assert.match(html, /<button type=\\\"submit\\\" disabled>Save notes<\\\\/button>/);\\n    assert.equal((await post('/projects/1/tasks/1/notes', { ...state, notes: 'Blocked' })).status, 403);\\n    await server.stop();\\n    server = undefined;\\n    const stored = new DatabaseSync(dbPath);\\n    const tasks = stored.prepare('SELECT * FROM tasks ORDER BY id').all();\\n    assert.equal(tasks[0].notes, notes);\\n    assert.equal(tasks[1].notes, '');\\n    assert.equal(tasks[2].notes, '');\\n    for (const key of ['id', 'project_id', 'completed', 'priority', 'due_date', 'position']) {\\n      assert.equal(tasks[0][key], original[0][key]);\\n    }\\n    const { notes: empty, ...second } = tasks[1];\\n    assert.equal(empty, '');\\n    assert.deepEqual(second, original[1]);\\n    stored.close();\\n    server = await start(dbPath);\\n    assert.ok((await get('/projects/1')).includes(escapedNotes(notes)));\\n    await post('/projects/1/restore', {});\\n    html = await get('/projects/1');\\n    assert.match(html, /<textarea id=\\\"task-notes-1\\\" name=\\\"notes\\\" rows=\\\"4\\\">/);\\n    await post('/projects/1/tasks/1/notes', { notes: '' });\\n    assert.match(await get('/projects/1'), /<textarea id=\\\"task-notes-1\\\" name=\\\"notes\\\" rows=\\\"4\\\"><\\\\/textarea>/);\\n    await post('/projects/1/tasks/2/notes', { notes: '  \\\\n\\\\t ' });\\n    await server.stop();\\n    server = undefined;\\n    const cleared = new DatabaseSync(dbPath);\\n    assert.equal(cleared.prepare('SELECT notes FROM tasks WHERE id = 1').get().notes, '');\\n    assert.equal(cleared.prepare('SELECT notes FROM tasks WHERE id = 2').get().notes, '  \\\\n\\\\t ');\\n    cleared.close();\\n  } finally {\\n    if (server) await server.stop();\\n    await rm(dir, { recursive: true, force: true });\\n  }\\n});\\n\"}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"read","description":"Read the contents of a file. Supports text files and images (jpg, png, gif, webp, bmp). Images are sent as attachments. For text files, output is truncated to 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). Use offset/limit for large files. When you need the full file, continue with offset until complete.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","offset","limit"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to read (relative or absolute)"},"offset":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number","description":"Line number to start reading from (1-indexed)"},{"type":"null"}]},"limit":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of lines to read"},{"type":"null"}]}},"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":true},{"type":"function","name":"bash","description":"Execute a bash command in the current working directory. Returns stdout and stderr. Output is truncated to last 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). If truncated, full output is saved to a temp file. Optionally provide a timeout in seconds.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["command","timeout"],"properties":{"command":{"type":"string","description":"Shell command to execute"},"timeout":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number","description":"Timeout in seconds (optional, no default timeout)"},{"type":"null"}]}},"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":true},{"type":"function","name":"edit","description":"Edit a single file using exact text replacement. Every edits[].oldText must match a unique, non-overlapping region of the original file. If two changes affect the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead of emitting overlapping edits. Do not include large unchanged regions just to connect distant changes.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","edits"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to edit (relative or absolute)"},"edits":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["oldText","newText"],"properties":{"oldText":{"type":"string","description":"Exact text for one targeted replacement. It must be unique in the original file and must not overlap with any other edits[].oldText in the same call."},"newText":{"type":"string","description":"Replacement text for this targeted edit."}},"additionalProperties":false},"description":"One or more targeted replacements. Each edit is matched against the original file, not incrementally. Do not include overlapping or nested edits. If two changes touch the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead."}},"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":true},{"type":"function","name":"write","description":"Write content to a file. Creates the file if it doesn't exist, overwrites if it does. Automatically creates parent directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","content"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to write (relative or absolute)"},"content":{"type":"string","description":"Content to write to the file"}},"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":true}],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":true,"prompt_cache_key":"608e1bec-26ad-43d9-928d-ad769992b3a9","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"low"},"top_p":0.98,"top_logprobs":0,"temperature":1.0,"reasoning":{"effort":"medium","summary":"detailed","context":"all_turns","mode":"standard"},"user":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":16841,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2016,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":77},"total_tokens":18857,"attribution":{"items":{"fc_02f3897e339f7ae7016acba6279fe887d1a6575e4b9427cddf":{"input_tokens":34,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_02f3897e339f7ae7016acba62b64e487d1b48b0227527061f1":{"input_tokens":28,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_02f3897e339f7ae7016acba62da04487d1ac5e57203fda25a0":{"input_tokens":28,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_02f3897e